        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪ್ರತಿಭಟಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರತಿಭಟಿಸು — pratibhaṭisu — \"to protest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಿದ್ಯಾರ್ಥಿಗಳು ಶುಲ್ಕ ಏರಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರತಿಭಟಿಸಿದರು. vidyārthigaḷu śulka ērikeyannu pratibhaṭisidaru. The students protested the rise in fees."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಪ್ರತಿಭಟಿಸಿದೆ, pratibhaṭiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರತಿಭಟನೆ, a protest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರತಿಭಟಿಸು (pratibhaṭisu) is built on Sanskrit pratibhaṭa, \"a match for, rivalling\" (Monier-Williams), with the Kannada verb ending -isu: to stand up against."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
